ct, a seat that leans Republican by about eight points. He faces Democrat Lakesha Womack, who has raised roughly $25,000 and reported negative cash on hand, while Moore has built a war chest above $1.5 million and drawn modest outside support.\n\nMost expert raters place the race between Likely R and Safe R, and prediction markets give Moore roughly an 88% chance of winning. The only public poll, a Republican-sponsored March survey of likely voters, showed Moore ahead by eight points. Moore has spent the fall touting FEMA funding for Helene recovery and bipartisan legislation, reinforcing his incumbent profile in a district favorable to him.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0644, "margin": -9.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0543, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0536, "margin": -11.0}]}